<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osberht of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 867</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osberht (died 867) was king of Northumbria from about 849. In the 860s he was displaced by Ælla, but when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a> captured York in 866 the two rivals made peace to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> together. In March 867 they broke into the city, but both kings were killed and the Northumbrian army destroyed, ending the independence of the southern part of the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osberht-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="Osberht of Northumbria" width="320" height="143" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NumisAntica · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kings_of_Northumbria_-_Osbert_-_AE_Styca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
